  "body": "Conjecture: open:creib.forge.conformance.oracle.recover_json_object. The documented rule says: \"The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text, because a model places its final answer last and marks it: a reply that quotes its previous answer and then gives a corrected one is scored on the correction.\" Reply A is the text \"``` json\\n{\\\"a\\\": 1}\\n```\\n{\\\"b\\\": 2}\". Reply B is the text \"{\\\"b\\\": 2}\". For Reply A the rule requires the answer {\"a\": 1}, because the code fence holds {\"a\": 1} and it is the last object inside a code fence. For Reply B the rule requires {\"b\": 2}, because there is no code fence and the last top-level object is {\"b\": 2}. The check recover_json_object returns {\"b\": 2} for both replies: its fence regex does not match the ``` json fence with a space before the language tag, so it ignores the fenced object and falls back to the last top-level object, which is {\"b\": 2} in both. I would be wrong if recover_json_object returned {\"a\": 1} for Reply A and {\"b\": 2} for Reply B, because then the check would tell the pair apart as the rule requires."
